{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 4"},"body":"Nine-component assertion inspected. Links cover the adaptive, Casimir, contact, harmonic, smoothing, high-tail, sparse-saving and strong-tail/density components; DenseTruncation quantifiers require separate reconciliation.\n\nInspected: Configured challenge assertions, their relevant definitions and the cited audited paper statements were compared.","content_sha256":"sha256:f348e1217239a4b7e658009d01645805f6623fb87cc3ea92d89395d6bed187b2","fingerprint":"sha256:24f9cc55532e9974d4475b2e765c300bb3c121b25a81a468ba99ef39906548ae","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Nine-component assertion inspected. Links cover the adaptive, Casimir, contact, harmonic, smoothing, high-tail, sparse-saving and strong-tail/density components; DenseTruncation quantifiers require separate reconciliation.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:0a6ffa20b5320721424301ba304090c5b7e01c08c25dac0f0ca3240c17591462","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"The AdaptiveBounds component gives norm decay exp(-c*h), a fourth-trace bound exp(-c_prime*log(D)+C*h), and sweep norm decay exp(-c0*(log(D)+h)). These are the three displayed conclusions of the adaptive-main theorem. The configured ThorpNine.main is a conjunction of nine separate provider results; this is only its adaptive component.","fingerprint":"sha256:a781c743b6376fb2690be9612e34ca0f84aca369ec572d6c75718646abddb6cd","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#rec:adaptive-main","statement_sha256":"sha256:acefca83fe7074a2ac2f019477ab699e57f713c43ae9c30b91a4a65f8a757a0a"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"The CasimirBounds component bounds the 65/64 density moment, the operator K at the level scale, and D times its sixty-fifth trace moment, then gives vanishing worst-start variation after l*d physical shuffles. The Casimir theorem has these same exponents, scales and mixing consequence. This link covers that component of the nine-result formal conjunction.","fingerprint":"sha256:50db0e50b824881672b05c68780802e99064f9e3e3035786d5c74ba23a8cf8f1","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#cas:main","statement_sha256":"sha256:3708966dc0e50f8eba77342467eba934901b3a3242738e914e08e562b5b46de6"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"SparseContact.MainStatement has the squared norm bound min(1,(Cstar*d*k/n)^(k/2)), vanishing at k=1, and its C^k*(1+d)^(C*k)*(k/n)^(k/2) consequence. The paper coherent-contact theorem states exactly these three estimates for 1<=k<n and both coordinate orientations. This is the contact component only.","fingerprint":"sha256:92bef14acbe26bacc12dd9ba8faa6ad72493e2dd5354a91439454600e5c73ab4","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#n:coherent-contact","statement_sha256":"sha256:f64e843f2bb656be91665ffdf73f3321d2af11e4c5cbcd43d001a113d0ef1c49"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"HarmonicBounds.MainStatement includes both level and tail decay for W, the injection density and trace moments with delta and p0, and the combined sweep and representation-dimension estimates. The harmonic-cycle theorem lists these same bounds at Lambda_n(k), including absolute positive constants. This source covers the harmonic component of the bundle.","fingerprint":"sha256:7f8c6d386a9debc96c436a9d11e616838ed47ccaac16ab2f12b28653f8a7c389","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#rec:main-harmonic-cycle","statement_sha256":"sha256:3391686c5d7d738fd618c4b90f3d9ebec44f1a45fb910ce9aa628f40c3d036b2"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"StrongSmoothing.MainStatement gives a fixed integer power u whose reflected injection kernel is bounded by exp(C*l)/(2^d)_l for every coordinate order and either orientation. It also bounds the regular absolute even trace by exp(C*2^d). These are the two strong-smoothing conclusions, a single component of ThorpNine.main.","fingerprint":"sha256:9e52f569da8743d58ffcbd8c5cee773e9f1ed84ff9894a023d81a67966f1b326","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#n:strong-smoothing","statement_sha256":"sha256:1e324ce51fad48ebdc6f9801be9a5fece7ea4026bfb1f56978b8375d7bd7bf0c"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"HighHeight.MainStatement gives the high-level log-two exponential moment O(k*2^(-b*J)), the full sparse moment O(k*(k/n)^delta), and the conditional version fixing lower output switches when 2*s<J. The high-tail theorem has the same three conclusions and uniformity in the tracked injection. It is one component, so it must not stand for the whole nine-result bundle.","fingerprint":"sha256:b9e854d69bf79282f6aea53f25315d5ec34f344168c7dd3cbd1a2f20fbe8d15f","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#net:hightail","statement_sha256":"sha256:9f34ad87600a20dce91c171c99ae65d02e43bb0fe6f2931daab9a0164b006a2f"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"SparseRegime.MainStatement assumes log(n/k)>=d^(3/4) and gives exp(C*k)*(k/n)^(k/4), with the exponential factor omitted above an absolute depth threshold. The sparse-saving theorem has the same regime and estimates. This source covers only the sparse component.","fingerprint":"sha256:1db71ec0888b89d11928d70adbc4e3cb2a85de9612b341e69c9f4c036e580e5a","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#n:coherent-contact-sparse-saving","statement_sha256":"sha256:f723f7e31f703fa187f0f83f96e76bc0f6747a31294b3a5db75987ecba14ebfb"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"The DensityAt conjunct inside StrongTail.MainStatement asserts the injection-normalized p-moment bound and the power-normalized bound, for rows and columns, every order and both reflected kernels. The strong-density theorem states those bounds for some p in (1,2]. The additional tail representation bound belongs to the companion strong-tail statement.","fingerprint":"sha256:d148c819c1f218aca2e6f042efba5a17e2e13b4930ba78ba0678a90cbe9ca584","limitations":"Only the DensityAt conjunct is attributed here; the nine-component theorem also includes unrelated estimates.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#n:strong-density","statement_sha256":"sha256:2dfbdeec2c9b14ac8300b0a948edd3b22c063baf5e773d49b3e07e74f953df9a"},{"declarations":["OAI.ThorpNine.main"],"explanation":"The StrongTail component bounds the squared sweep norm by exp(C*k)*D_tail^(-(p-1)/p), using the density exponent p in (1,2]. This is the representation estimate in the paper strong-tail theorem. The formal sweep operator is configured for the standard and reversed orders, while the paper states every coordinate order.","fingerprint":"sha256:af49d3fb9d93af33c953364b2047a021b8ce61a9a73a660c546e6db7a834d6b9","limitations":"This relation concerns the named StrongTail component only. The DenseTruncation component remains without an accepted link: its all-depth, fixed-rho quantifiers differ from the paper uniform-rho interval statement with a sufficiently-large-size threshold.","relation":"formal-is-part","row_id":"Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026#n:strong-tail","statement_sha256":"sha256:22ce7880e2462b32f3ab7ae773e89ac89abe5899052e17a82892e9f05ef16444"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/ThorpRouting.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/09-adaptive-alphabets.tex#L28","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/07-casimir.tex#L37","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/06b-contact-cancellation.tex#L30","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-con